  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed front roof extensions, by reason of their scale, form and siting, would introduce an incongruous and visually intrusive form of development that would fail to relate appropriately to the traditional pitched roof form of the host terrace. The development would result in significant harm to the architectural integrity and established character of the terrace and wider street scene. The proposal represents poor design that would not be visually well integrated within its context. The development is therefore contrary to Policies LP1 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the guidance set out in the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
